WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 6.4 · MEAL: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning
Baselines and targets

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
When you are starting out, the starting point is now: capture it before your work begins.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.393
A baseline is the value of an indicator before your work starts. A target is the value you aim to reach by a given date. Together they let you show change and judge progress.

4
00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:28.393
Two numbers and the steps between

5
00:00:28.393 --> 00:00:39.352
Baseline: Where things stand at the start, or your plan to find out. For example: Asked at sign-up: 2 of 12 youth club members have done volunteer work.

6
00:00:39.352 --> 00:00:48.830
Target: Where you aim to be, and by when. For example: Provisional: 8 of 12 members volunteering by the end of the first year.

7
00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:59.507
Milestones: Quarterly steps towards an annual target, where that helps you manage. For example: Three volunteering by March, five by June, eight by December.

8
00:00:59.907 --> 00:01:00.507
Why they matter

9
00:01:00.507 --> 00:01:04.700
1. Without a baseline you cannot show change.

10
00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:10.004
2. Without a target you cannot judge whether progress is enough.

11
00:01:10.004 --> 00:01:17.419
3. When you start something new, now is the best moment to capture it.

12
00:01:17.819 --> 00:01:18.419
How you will use them

13
00:01:18.419 --> 00:01:23.352
1. Your monitoring: actual results compared with targets each period.

14
00:01:23.352 --> 00:01:29.026
2. Your evaluation: the baseline is the point you measure change from.

15
00:01:29.026 --> 00:01:35.330
3. Your reports and claims: honest figures with their starting point.

16
00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:36.330
What to avoid

17
00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:41.633
Inventing a baseline: write “to be established by [date]” instead.

18
00:01:41.633 --> 00:01:46.567
Reading too much into a percentage from six people.

19
00:01:46.567 --> 00:01:52.500
Changing targets quietly instead of openly, with a reason.

20
00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.900
You set baselines, or plans to establish them, and targets.

21
00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:58.900
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:03.500
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
